; BlindCreations.inix -- how this database opens, and how each table is heard.
;
; BlindCreations gathers the Blind directories -- apps, books, creators and presentations made by blind people --
; into one database to search, filter, sort, mark and play. It began with a proposal on the BITS development list
; for one searchable place for software and books by or for blind people. DbDo's developer rebuilds it from the
; directories with scripts\buildBlindCreations; your own copy is yours to add to.
;
; DbDo reads this file beside the database. ; Look is each table's default columns and prime its default order (5 November 2026); a table's
; saved columns, order and filter are written here only when a person chooses them, except an order
; that runs newest first, which prime cannot say.
; [Database] decides which table the window starts on; each
; [Table:<name>] decides which columns the grid shows, in which order, and how the rows are sorted. DbDo writes these
; keys back whenever you change the columns, the sort or the filter, so what you adjust is remembered here.
;
; A row is heard, not seen: three fields, the deciding one first, and the first column is the one you look a record
; up by, since typing a letter searches it.
;
; WHO MADE WHAT is recorded in the maps table: a creator is author_of a book, developer_of an app, or
; presenter_of a presentation. Shift+R says a record's links, and Alt+Right follows one. The by field also names the
; makers, so a row says who made it and Keywords finds people too.

[Database]

; THE WINDOW OPENS ON apps: software was the proposal's first want, and Choose Table, Control+T, reaches the rest.
InitialTable = apps

[Table:apps]

; name, then category, then platform: what it is, what it is for, where it runs. The platform answers the
; proposal's question of operating system; Control+F, Fields, narrows by it.
; SelectFields, 13 October 2026: who made it is the point of this database, so it is heard second.

[Table:books]

; title, then author, then year, the way a reader asks for a book.
; SelectFields, 13 October 2026: the form a book comes in -- braille, audio, print -- tells a reader more than its year.

[Table:creators]

; surname, then first name, then roles -- author, developer, presenter -- so typing a letter finds a person by
; surname, as in the directories.

[Table:presentations]

; title, then presenter, then kind: a podcast, a broadcast, a talk or keynote, a video series.

; Saved view settings moved from the retired views table (describeFields, 4 November 2026).
[Table:apps]
SelectFields = name, category, platform
[Table:apps]
OrderFields = name
[Table:books]
SelectFields = title, by, year
[Table:books]
OrderFields = title
[Table:creators]
SelectFields = last_name, first_name, roles
[Table:creators]
OrderFields = last_name, first_name
[Table:presentations]
SelectFields = title, by, kind
[Table:presentations]
OrderFields = title
